// Title: Potential Persistence Via Netsh Helper DLL - Registry
// Sigma ID: c90362e0-2df3-4e61-94fe-b37615814cb1
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Anish Bogati
// Date: 2023-11-28 | Modified: 2025-10-08
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, persistence, T1546.007
// Description: Detects changes to the Netsh registry key to add a new DLL value. This change might be an
//   indication of a potential persistence attempt by adding a malicious Netsh helper
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate helper added by different programs and the OS
// References:
//   - https://www.ired.team/offensive-security/persistence/t1128-netsh-helper-dll
//   - https://pentestlab.blog/2019/10/29/persistence-netsh-helper-dll/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_netsh_helper_dll_potential_persistence.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where (RegistryKey contains "\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\NetSh" and RegistryValueData contains ".dll") and (not((InitiatingProcessFolderPath =~ "C:\\Windows\\System32\\poqexec.exe" and (RegistryValueData in~ ("ipmontr.dll", "iasmontr.dll", "ippromon.dll")))))
